# Legacy simplex fixture/demo over three authored locomotion anchors.
# Canonical presentation and CTest demo: demo_walk_2d.pmg_spec.
# Demonstrates:
# - a 2-D ParametricMotionSpace with measured metric calibration;
# - the minimum three non-collinear examples needed for local 2-D lookup;
# - interpolation and runtime requests over the authored simplex.
# This demonstrates simplex support enforcement.
# Does not demonstrate:
# - full rectangular motion coverage or a tight-turn jog endpoint;
# - independent turn and speed control across the whole domain;
# - a robust production locomotion family.
#
# Axis 0: authored turn class (0 = wide, 1 = tight).
# Axis 1: authored gait class (0 = walk, 1 = jog).
# The authored labels are categorical anchors; parameter_metrics calibrates
# generated behavior against measured turn rate and travel speed.
node walk_2d 2
registration walk_2d - - 3 0
parameter_metrics walk_2d turn_rate travel_speed
parameter_calibration walk_2d 5
parameter_support walk_2d simplex
example walk_2d 0.0 0.0 ../BVH/walkCurve.bvh
example walk_2d 1.0 0.0 ../BVH/walkTightCurve.bvh start_frame 33 end_frame 67 phase_label left_contact_start contact_start L=contact;R=swing contact_end L=contact;R=swing
example walk_2d 0.0 1.0 ../BVH/jogCurve.bvh start_frame 23 end_frame 46 phase_label left_contact_start contact_start L=contact;R=swing contact_end L=contact;R=swing
# Both axes vary, so this is a genuine 2-D space -- held to that claim at load.
expect walk_2d spanned_axes 2
# The authored support is the triangle formed by the three examples above.
# LoadGraphSpec validates that the examples are exactly a non-collinear simplex.
# corner_coverage full is deliberately NOT claimed: the (1,1) tight-jog corner
# is unsampled because the corpus has only one jog clip (jogCurve). A complete
# rectangular 2-D family would add a tight-turn jog BVH. Until then, requests
# outside the authored triangle are projected onto the valid simplex and synthesize
# sparse three-example blends.
edge walk_2d walk_2d
# Explicit default advancing phase range. This does not enforce triangular
# support; it only fixes where the transition metric searches within cycles.
edge_phase_range walk_2d walk_2d 0.70 0.95 0.05 0.30
edge_config walk_2d walk_2d 300 400 3 6 41
